  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<p>Correct answer: B</p>\n<p>B: Magnetic force magnitude is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F=qvB\\sin\\theta\"></span>. For motion parallel to the field, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\theta=0\"></span> so <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F=qvB\\sin 0=0\"></span>.</p>\n<p>C: This would apply only if <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\theta=90^\\circ\"></span> (motion perpendicular to the field). Here <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\theta=0\"></span> so the force is zero.</p>\n<p>D: The correct dependence is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F=qvB\\sin\\theta\"></span>, not <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"qvB\\cos\\theta\"></span>. For <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\theta=0\"></span>, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\sin\\theta=0\"></span> so <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F=0\"></span>.</p>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_1a",
  "question": {
